---
description: Keep form controls one height and toolbars wrapping without stranding actions
alwaysApply: true
---

# Control height and toolbars

Single-line controls share `--control-h` (44px): inputs, selects, and `.btn`. Set `height` and `min-height` to that token. Do not invent a one-off height for a new field or button.

Textareas, segment chips, and table text actions are the exceptions. Change those only when that component is intentionally a different control, and say so next to the rule.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — button shorter than the search field beside it */
.btn { min-height: 40px; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.btn, input, select { height: var(--control-h); min-height: var(--control-h); }
```

Toolbars (`.toolbar`) wrap as a row. Search and filters stay in the row; `.actions` uses `margin-left: auto` so the button group sits on the trailing edge of whatever line it lands on. Do not use a flex spacer to push those buttons; a spacer collapses on wrap and pins the buttons to the left.

Below 640px, search, each filter, and the action group each take the full row. Action buttons share that row instead of overflowing the page.
